## Context
Child of tracker 1153, blocked by 1160 (stack order). The callers of gaze and verify-gate must agree on one contract once gaze stops gating.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] raid, merge, hunt, dashboard, verify-gate and rules/git.md agree: no gate after a gaze ESCALATE or a missing or stale result; callers own gate sessions (one UUID per PR, same `session=` on round 1 and the single re-gate, one two-round cap on every path including the permission-denial recovery); the gate makes its own worktree
- [ ] The caller closes the ticket on the branch before gating, and the merge prerequisite is one line: the gate's `ruled_tip_sha` equals the branch head, else re-gate; one field name everywhere
- [ ] raid owns the fix-and-regate loop with gaze's old guards (10-minute timeout, red test first, test budget with pre-push gate, ESCALATE when the gate disagrees with the reviewers)
- [ ] grep-proven: no live caller still keys on an APPROVED gaze; PR under the 15-file breaker; catalog drift clean
